    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393-a6">

                <pb facs="0453" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg403"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 275.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Gray.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Merida, Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have thus far delayed responding to your
                    dispatch of February 12, 1894, with inclosures from the Secretary of Treasury
                    requesting information concerning discriminating rebates, etc., in favor of
                    Mexican vessels, in the hope of soon being able to formulate a reply based upon
                    official records. This, however, I have not yet been able to do. Mean <pb
                        facs="0454" n="404" xml:id="pg404"/> while I beg to advise you that, from
                    all the information I have been able to procure from ship masters and agents, as
                    well as from inquiries prosecuted by John Waddle, consular agent at Progreso, a
                    copy of whose letter bearing date March 19, 1894, I herewith inclose, I am
                    satisfied that no such discrimination as is contemplated in your dispatch or its
                    inclosures exists in my consular district.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. L. Davis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
